# scripts/dev-fix-auditor-durability-step0b-detection-redispatch2-to-review.jq
#
# FIX-AUDITOR-DURABILITY-STEP0B-DETECTION — developer response to QA
# CHANGES_REQUESTED (redispatch_count=1). Row already lives in
# .task_board.review[] (no lane move needed) — updates it in place with the
# new fix + live-fire evidence and hands back to qa for independent
# re-verification (same "narrates vs executes" risk class this exact row's
# own history already exposed once — self-certification to DONE_VERIFIED is
# NOT taken here on purpose).
#
# Usage:
#   jq --arg now "$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)" \
#     -f scripts/dev-fix-auditor-durability-step0b-detection-redispatch2-to-review.jq \
#     docs/data/orch/orch-state.json | bash scripts/orch-apply.sh

(.task_board.review | map(.id == "FIX-AUDITOR-DURABILITY-STEP0B-DETECTION") | index(true)) as $idx
| if $idx == null then error("FIX-AUDITOR-DURABILITY-STEP0B-DETECTION not found in .task_board.review[]") else . end
| .task_board.review[$idx] += {
    status: "REVIEW",
    next_agent: "qa",
    reviewed_at: $now,
    reviewed_by: "developer",
    review_note: "Response to QA CHANGES_REQUESTED (redispatch_count=1). RAW-verified current state FIRST per dispatch instruction (baseline had shifted since QA's review): the 2 specific orphaned markers QA cited (2026-08-06T21:09:00Z / 2026-08-07T00:00Z) were already gone — deleted by an UNRELATED manual housekeeping commit 75d51f17a (2026-08-12, \"auditor housekeeping — ledgers, tool-usage stats, cycle marker rotation\"), bypassing Step 0b.1 entirely (zero D-CYCLE-1 ledger entry for either tick, confirming they were never actually swept by the detector). Tier-3's cited 52h35m gap was also already closed by an unrelated fix (FIX-AUDITOR-T1-T3-CLEANEXIT-HEARTBEAT-STAMP-SKIPPED-T2-UNAFFECTED, 2026-08-12) that made the heartbeat write actually reach disk — tier-3 last_healthy_at is now fresh (~23h gap at time of this fix, well within the 48h bar). ROOT CAUSE (found by building+testing real code, not narration): despite the 2026-08-14 FIX-AUDITOR-NOTEBOOK-COMPOSE-ACTUATOR-BUILT-TESTED-NEVER-WIRED commit upgrading Step 0b.1 from narrated-prose to syntactically-real inline bash, the detector STILL never fired — confirmed via 14 real orphaned marker files (2026-08-11 through 2026-08-14, spanning ~160+ missed Tier-1 sweep opportunities) still unswept at this fix's start, zero D-CYCLE-1/D-CYCLE-2 signals anywhere. That 08-14 fix closed a DIFFERENT gap (prose->real code) but never changed the INVOCATION mechanism: an inline ~65-line bash block early in a 1400+ line flow doc has no forcing function compelling an LLM subagent to actually invoke Bash on it every cycle, and nothing downstream could ever notice a skipped cycle — same narrates-vs-executes class as FIX-LEAF-AGENT-ANALYSIS-ONLY-EXIT-NARRATES-INSTEAD-OF-EXECUTING, whose own scope (per that fix and per QA) was OUTPUT-CONTRACT/RETURN only, never this Step 0b area. FIX APPLIED: (1) Step 0b.1+0b.2 extracted wholesale into a new tested actuator script, scripts/auditor-durability-sweep.sh (429L incl. header), following the SAME proven call-once-not-narrate pattern this file already uses for Notebook Write (notebook-compose.sh) and OUTPUT-CONTRACT (audit-output-contract.sh) -- main.md now makes ONE mandatory tool call instead of hand-transcribing inline bash. New companion scripts/auditor-durability-sweep.test.sh, 29/29 passing, shellcheck clean, sources emit-audit-signal.sh directly (mcp_call stub seam, zero real network calls in the suite) rather than subprocess-invoking it, matching that script's own documented composability precedent. (2) NEW mandatory never-omit [DURABILITY-SWEEP] RETURN-block line (narration half) PLUS a new scripts/audit-output-contract.sh --require-durability-sweep flag (V8 check, purely additive/opt-in, wired unconditionally into main.md's single OUTPUT-CONTRACT call site) -- V8 checks $MARKERS_FILE for the mandatory [durability-sweep] summary line and fires a VIOLATION if absent, closing the invisibility gap so a FUTURE skipped invocation is mechanically caught, not just narrated. audit-output-contract.test.sh gains T28-T30 (94/94 total passing, zero regression on the 91 pre-existing cases). (3) SECOND independent latent bug found+fixed while building real tested code: jq's fromdateiso8601 cannot parse the notebook heading's minute-precision timestamp (no seconds) -- the ORIGINAL prose spec's own \"same fromdateiso8601 idiom\" comment called for exactly this broken form, meaning even a cycle that had faithfully hand-executed the old bash would have silently lost the \"OR the heartbeat with the notebook heading\" half of the Tier-1 fallback check on every single run since 2026-08-06, invisibly. Fixed with the same to_epoch idiom already established in emit-audit-signal.sh/audit-output-contract.sh for exactly this bug class (T8b covers it). (4) .gitignore gains an entry for docs/agent-memory/.auditor-cycle-markers-*.tmp (mirrors the sibling docs/data/cycle-snapshot-*.json.tmp pattern) + git rm --cached on all 7 then-tracked marker-file copies, restoring the \"rm -f is a safe reclaim\" invariant the source architecture brief specified. LIVE FIRE (not just \"logic looks correct\" -- QA already found that insufficient once on this exact row): ran scripts/auditor-durability-sweep.sh for real against the live repo. Result: found=14 swept=14 malformed=4 schedule_gap_t1=0 schedule_gap_t2=0 schedule_gap_t3=0 (zero schedule-gap fire is CORRECT given the baseline-shift above -- all 3 heartbeats are genuinely fresh right now, confirmed independently via direct file reads before firing). 11 real D-CYCLE-1 signal_queue rows landed with real ids (sys-20260815T021802-7b3a through sys-20260815T021825-6e05, type=auditor_cycle_loss, all confirmed present in orch-state.json .signal_queue.rows[] + docs/data/auditor-dedup-ledger.json post-fire) and their 11 marker files were genuinely rm -f'd from disk. The remaining 3 (all malformed-key class: 2 colon-bearing auditor-t1: files, 1 empty-key file, 1 seconds-bearing malformed-timestamp file) hit the LIVE mcp-server's own independent near-duplicate-payload dedup on post_agent_signal (4 near-identical D-CYCLE-1/malformed-key calls within ~6s -- 1st succeeded, next 3 got success:false/e1-not-written) -- correctly left in place per this sweep's own documented ABORT-preserves-evidence design (never delete the only evidence of a loss on a failed emit), will retry on the next real Tier-1 cycle. This server-side near-duplicate throttle is a pre-existing, separate mechanism, not a defect introduced by this fix. D-CYCLE-2 was NOT live-fired (all 3 heartbeats genuinely healthy right now, so nothing SHOULD fire) -- the schedule-gap detection logic itself is proven via T5/T6/T8 synthetic-fixture tests instead (stale-heartbeat trigger + fresh-heartbeat non-trigger, both directions, both confirmed). Commits: [FILLED AFTER COMMIT]. Does NOT self-certify DONE_VERIFIED -- this exact row's own history is the narrates-vs-executes recurring-risk class; independent QA re-verification requested per that precedent, same as the original submission."
  }
| .task_board._updated_at = $now
| .task_board._updated_by = "developer (FIX-AUDITOR-DURABILITY-STEP0B-DETECTION redispatch 2 response)"
